I sat in my seat on the train and looked around.
A stressed father sat opposite me.
He brought his two small children.
The father had a big book.
He really wanted to read his book.
But he did not get much peace.
His daughter had a red ball.
His son had a green toy car.
The children were very restless.
They constantly threw their toys on the floor.
The father sighed loudly and closed his book.
He picked the things up from the floor.
He gave the children their toys back.
"You must sit quietly," he said tiredly.
He opened his book again.
Two minutes later, the ball fell on the floor.
It hit the father's left shoe.
The man picked up the ball again.
I smiled at the tired father.
He just shook his head and looked down into his book.
